  annotation "note_1771590162218_0", anchor: "Built the shrine Ritus∴um to contain it — from fear, not reverence", text: "Ritus∴um is not a shrine. It is a commemorative gathering — held at The Drowned Ledge, governed by witness-obligation, requiring offerings of captured fire. I conflated the container with the ceremony and then decorated the error with a neat binary. \"Fear, not reverence\" is the kind of clean distinction the Nightshelf would find incomprehensible. Their entire ritual vocabulary treats fear as the *precondition* for reverence. Sloppy sentence. Sloppy thinking.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590162218_1", anchor: "Unknown; held it after Gork's death", text: "The Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane killed Gork in the corrupted thermal chambers. The Guild then held the artifact. The transfer between those two facts — from the Augur's flippers to the Guild's custody — receives no scrutiny anywhere in the source material. \"Unknown\" is my honest assessment. It is not an acceptable one. Someone carried a catastrophically dangerous relic out of a corruption zone and delivered it to a trade faction. That someone had a name and a reason.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590162218_2", anchor: "reach beneath the frozen sea", text: "An artifact that projects silence into the deep, now strapped to the ribs of a raider whose theology requires waking a sleeping god beneath that same water. \"Unusual restraint\" is one reading. Operational prudence is another.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
